

[38;5;231m⏺[39m Section 3 of 3 — [1mthe wired preference, and testing[0m.

  The preference is [38;5;153mtheme[39m (light/dark). One thing to be straight about: the page has [3mno[0m CSS today, so wiring a theme
  necessarily introduces a stylesheet. That's a real cost of this choice, not something I can design away — but it stays
  small. A new [38;5;153mstyles.css[39m defines two custom properties on [38;5;153m:root[39m, overridden under [38;5;153m[data-theme="dark"][39m, applied to
  [38;5;153mbody[39m. Roughly fifteen lines, no design system, no component styling.

  The wiring in [38;5;153mapp.js[39m:

  - [38;5;153mapplyTheme()[39m sets [38;5;153mdocument.documentElement.dataset.theme[39m from [38;5;153mPrefs.get("theme")[39m.
  - On load, it runs once [1mand[0m initializes the toggle's [38;5;153mchecked[39m state from the same stored value. Both, not just the
    first — applying the theme while leaving the control showing its HTML default is the standard bug here, and it reads
    to the user as "my setting didn't save."
  - A [38;5;153mchange[39m listener on the toggle calls [38;5;153mPrefs.set(...)[39m then [38;5;153mapplyTheme()[39m.

  The control is a [38;5;153m<label><input type="checkbox" id="theme-toggle"> Dark mode</label>[39m placed [1moutside[0m [38;5;153m#login-form[39m, so it
  can't participate in form submission. The existing submit handler, [38;5;153mlogin()[39m, and [38;5;153mvalidateForm()[39m are untouched.

  Tests ([38;5;153mtest/prefs.test.js[39m, [38;5;153mnode --test[39m) cover the module against a fake storage: default when empty, round-trip of a
  valid value, default when the stored value is invalid, default when the JSON won't parse, default when the parsed root
  isn't an object, unknown keys preserved across a write, and no throw when [38;5;153mgetItem[39m/[38;5;153msetItem[39m themselves throw.

  [1mKnown gap, stated plainly:[0m the DOM wiring is not covered by automated tests — no jsdom, no e2e, per the tooling
  choice. Its verification is manual: open [38;5;153mindex.html[39m, toggle to dark, reload, confirm it persists.

  Files: [38;5;153mprefs.js[39m (new), [38;5;153mstyles.css[39m (new), [38;5;153mtest/prefs.test.js[39m (new), [38;5;153mindex.html[39m (two script/link tags plus the toggle),
  [38;5;153mapp.js[39m (apply-on-load and the listener), [38;5;153mpackage.json[39m (a [38;5;153mscripts.test[39m entry). [38;5;153msrc/[39m is untouched.

  That's the full design. If it looks right, I'll write it up as a spec — and to set expectations on what comes next: on
